course: dictionary
lesson: 11725
title: Available: can get it, or free to help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Available is an adjective with two meanings. It can mean you can get, buy or use a thing now. It can also mean a person is free to see you or help, not busy. «The last bag of crisps is still available in the shop.» The words in the shop tell you it means you can buy it.
explain: «Is the nurse available to see me now?» Here the nurse is not a thing, so available means free, not busy. Check by swapping in a word like free or ready to help. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Available means you can get it, buy it or use it now.
fact: Available can also mean a person is free to see you or help, not busy.
fact: In maths, «available money» or «available seats» tells you the limit you can use.
fact: The opposites of available are unavailable, sold out and busy.
fact: Use the words around available to decide which meaning fits: a shop, a thing, or a person.
exercise: «The last bag of crisps is available in the shop.» What does available mean? | *You can buy it now | It is too big | You are free to talk | It is far away
exercise: «Is the nurse available to see me now?» What does available mean here? | *Free, not busy | Lost and hard to find | Ready to be eaten | Sold out
exercise: A maths problem says, «You have 20 pounds available to spend.» What does available tell you? | *The limit you can use | The money is lost | The price of the toy | The shop is closed
test: «Only two tickets are still available for the show.» What does available mean? | The show was cancelled | Broken and useless | *Still on sale, you can get one
test: Which word is the opposite of available? | Free to help | *Sold out | Ready to use
exam: Maria asks, «Is the library book available?» What does she want to know? | How heavy it is | *Whether she can borrow it now | Whether it is green | Who wrote it
